cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How Well Does a Kepler-Trained Transit Classifier Transfer to TESS?
  A Characterization Study
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying study, please cite it
  using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Dhruv
    family-names: Ramani
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DhruvR-16/exoplanet_detection'
url: 'https://github.com/DhruvR-16/exoplanet_detection'
abstract: >-
  A physics-informed machine-learning pipeline for detecting transiting
  exoplanets in TESS photometry (Transit Least Squares, eight physical
  features, a calibrated RandomForest+XGBoost ensemble, and five orthogonal
  physics-vetting checks), together with a characterization study of its
  Kepler-to-TESS cross-mission transfer on a 500-target labeled benchmark.
keywords:
  - exoplanets
  - transit photometry
  - TESS
  - machine learning
  - cross-mission transfer
  - astronomy
